    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d557">

                <pb facs="0884" n="764" xml:id="pg764"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/3788</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thomas W.
                        Lamont</hi><anchor n="16" xml:id="d557-f1"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-04-07"><hi rendition="#italic">April 7,
                        1922</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received April 10.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Reverting to our
                    conversation of Wednesday concerning the Consortium for the assistance of China,
                    we have deemed it wise to address a private letter to the members of the
                    American Group, to the number of forty or thereabouts as indicated on this
                    letterhead, along the lines of the draft letter enclosed.<anchor n="17"
                        xml:id="d557-f2"/> Inasmuch, however, as we quote informally your expression
                    of opinion on this matter, we will not venture to transmit this letter to the
                    members until you have read it and have given us your sanction.</p>
                <p>Assuring you of our continued desire to cooperate with the Department, I am</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. W. Lamont</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d557-f1" n="16" type="source" xml:id="d557-f1-content">
                <p>Chairman of American group.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d557-f2" n="17" xml:id="d557-f2-content">
                <p>Draft letter not printed; it is identical with the letter from the managing
                    committee to the members of the American group, Apr. 24, 1922 (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg766">p. 766</ref>), except
                    for the addition of the penultimate paragraph of that letter which incorporates
                    the suggestions of the Secretary expressed in his letter printed <hi
                        rendition="#italic">infra.</hi></p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
